---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { INSTITUTION_COUNT, NETWORK_NAME, REVIEW_TIME } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" current="about">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the network</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Connecting Australian nutrition research</h1>

    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="text-lg">
        <mark>[CHECK]</mark> The {NETWORK_NAME} brings together Australian researchers working to understand why people
        respond differently to food, and how nutrition advice and care can be tailored to the individual. We connect
        nutrition scientists and dietitians with biomedical scientists, engineers, data scientists, statisticians and
        clinicians, and make it easier to find and reuse the valuable datasets that already exist.
      </p>

      <h2>Our aims</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Make existing Australian nutrition datasets easier to find and reuse, so that participants' contributions go further and studies are not repeated unnecessarily.</li>
        <li>Connect researchers across disciplines to build the teams that precision nutrition needs.</li>
        <li>Share practical know-how, such as protocols, templates and training recordings, among members.</li>
        <li>Support students and early-career researchers through mentoring and supervision links.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Researchers from {INSTITUTION_COUNT} Australian institutions have joined the network, spanning universities,
        medical research institutes and health services. <mark>[CHECK]</mark>
      </p>
      <p>
        The network is led by its <strong>leadership committee</strong>, which runs this website and reviews every
        listing. <mark>[CHECK: add committee members' names and roles here if you would like them listed.]</mark>
      </p>

      <h2>How moderation works</h2>
      <p>Every dataset and skills profile is checked by an admin from the leadership committee before it appears.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>You submit a listing. It is saved as pending and is not visible to anyone else.</li>
        <li>
          Within {REVIEW_TIME}, an admin checks that it describes data only (no files or details that could identify a
          participant), that the person submitting it is the custodian or has their permission, and whether participant
          consent covers secondary use.
        </li>
        <li>The admin approves the listing, or emails you with a question or the reason it can't be listed.</li>
        <li>Once approved, it appears in the directory with the date it was listed and last reviewed.</li>
        <li>Each year we ask custodians to confirm their listing is still current. Listings without a reply are taken down.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        You can update or remove your listing at any time. See <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>Privacy and terms</a> for
        how.
      </p>

      <h2>What the network does not do</h2>
      <p>
        The network does not hold, host or grant access to research data. Each listing describes data held by its
        custodian, who decides who can use it and on what terms, and who remains responsible for ethics approvals,
        participant consent and data agreements. A listing is not an endorsement of a dataset or a researcher.
      </p>

      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={withBase('/submit/')}>Submit a dataset</a> you are willing to share.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/submit/profile/')}>Join the skills directory</a> so collaborators can find you.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/resources/')}>Become a member</a> to access recordings, templates and protocols.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Contact the admins</a> with questions or ideas.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
